From: atomozero
Subject: EHCI: Prevent kernel panic on host system error during isochronous transfers

When the EHCI controller encounters a host system error (HSE), the
isochronous finish thread continues processing iTD descriptors that may
have been corrupted by the DMA failure. This causes a General Protection
Exception kernel panic when the thread dereferences invalid pointers.

The fix adds:
1. A volatile flag (fHostSystemError) set in the interrupt handler when
   HSE is detected
2. A check in FinishIsochronousTransfers() that breaks out of the
   processing loop when the flag is set, preventing access to
   potentially corrupted iTD memory
3. Cancellation of all pending isochronous transfers after HSE, so
   waiting threads don't hang indefinitely

Tested with USB webcam streaming (AUKEY PC-LM1E, isochronous MJPEG)
that reliably triggers HSE after 2-3 minutes on Intel EHCI controller
(Sony VAIO VPCEB3K1E, Intel Core i3 M370).

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.h b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.h
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.h
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.h
@@ -233,6 +233,7 @@
 		bool						fStopThreads;
+		volatile bool				fHostSystemError;
 		int32						fNextStartingFrame;

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
index abcdef2..1234568 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
@@ -XXX,6 +XXX,7 @@ (constructor - near fStopThreads initialization)
 	fStopThreads = false;
+	fHostSystemError = false;

@@ -1618,2 +1618,17 @@
-	if (status & EHCI_USBSTS_HOSTSYSERR)
-		TRACE_ERROR("host system error!\n");
+	if (status & EHCI_USBSTS_HOSTSYSERR) {
+		TRACE_ERROR("host system error!\n");
+		fHostSystemError = true;
+
+		// Wake up the isochronous finisher thread so it can abort
+		// gracefully instead of processing corrupted descriptors.
+		release_sem_etc(fFinishIsochronousTransfersSem, 1,
+			B_DO_NOT_RESCHEDULE);
+	}

@@ -2127,6 +2127,11 @@
 	while (!fStopThreads) {
 		// Go to sleep if there are no isochronous transfers to process
 		if (acquire_sem(fFinishIsochronousTransfersSem) != B_OK)
 			return;

+		// Check for host system error - do not process descriptors
+		// as the DMA engine may have corrupted iTD memory.
+		if (fHostSystemError) {
+			TRACE_ERROR("host system error detected, aborting "
+				"isochronous processing\n");
+			_CancelAllPendingIsochronousTransfers();
+			fHostSystemError = false;
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		bool transferDone = false;

@@ -2239,0 +2249,16 @@
+
+
+void
+EHCI::_CancelAllPendingIsochronousTransfers()
+{
+	if (!LockIsochronous())
+		return;
+
+	isochronous_transfer_data *transfer = fFirstIsochronousTransfer;
+	while (transfer != NULL) {
+		transfer->is_active = false;
+		transfer = transfer->link;
+	}
+
+	UnlockIsochronous();
+	TRACE_ERROR("cancelled all pending isochronous transfers\n");
+}
